From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jxlarrea <jx@jxl.me>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:06:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] ASoC: mediatek: amzn-spi-pcm: Fix the 8-channel status
 frame

With CONFIG_SND_SOC_8_MICS, eight ADC channels, dough_status_frame
declared rsvd0 twice, once with the 8-channel size and once with the
4-channel one, so no such build compiled. With eight ADC channels the
FPGA sends 15 reserved bytes, as in the Fire OS 6.5.7.1 Echo Dot kernel.
The Echo Dot (2nd gen) uses seven of them for its microphones.
---
 sound/soc/mediatek/mt_soc_audio_8163_amzn/amzn-spi-pcm/dough.h | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/mediatek/mt_soc_audio_8163_amzn/amzn-spi-pcm/dough.h b/sound/soc/mediatek/mt_soc_audio_8163_amzn/amzn-spi-pcm/dough.h
index c9287e03..b10bc4c7 100644
--- a/sound/soc/mediatek/mt_soc_audio_8163_amzn/amzn-spi-pcm/dough.h
+++ b/sound/soc/mediatek/mt_soc_audio_8163_amzn/amzn-spi-pcm/dough.h
@@ -33,7 +33,6 @@ struct dough_audio_frame {
 struct __attribute__((__packed__)) dough_status_frame {
 #if defined CONFIG_SND_SOC_8_MICS
 	uint8_t rsvd0[15];          /* bytes 12-26 */
-	uint8_t rsvd0[6];           /* bytes 12-17 */
 #elif defined CONFIG_SND_SOC_4_MICS
 	uint8_t rsvd0[6];           /* bytes 12-17 */
 #endif
